                <pb facs="0413" n="295" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg295"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.5048/56: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wharton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-08-03T14:00:00-00:44">August 3, 1929—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 4:15 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>37. Referring to my cable of July 26, midnight. Ross states that charges are
                    unfounded and he would welcome a full and complete investigation conditions of
                    Firestone labor.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wharton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
